From 8fecc9a4f1481762bdefff5c7a4e772eaca61e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmad Jalil <ahzs645@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:55:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(indoor): door-scoped native-cell owner review in the
 compile

prepareIndoorDataset takes an optional nativeDoorOwnerReview: a short list
of native doors with the two rooms each should join. Only those doors are
touched. Every other door, and every run without the option, is matched
exactly as before (same pre-landing snapshot as cb140e4 on the synthetic
projects in the test).

A listed door is connected only when all of this holds; otherwise the
compile throws with the reason:
- the door exists on the level with a precise footprint and normal;
- no reviewed door link names it (explicit reviews keep precedence);
- the legacy matcher, the physical-level labels and the automatic
  ownership recovery left it without a portal;
- the native-cell matcher, with its default steps and its fail-closed
  2 ft owner gap, decides two different walkable rooms in two different
  cells, at one floor height;
- those are exactly the two listed rooms.
No step, gap or override is configurable through the option.

The cells are built where the level's doors are matched, from the plane's
own exact native free floor (createNativeWalkingRegionQuery, the authority
the native circulation cells are cut from) minus every door threshold on
the plane, split along the reviewed access zones and named by the same
majority rule. They are not taken from room outlines. Faces with a staff
member or with no member carry no cell, so that side stays undecided.
Connector anchors do not exist yet at this stage; a face the finished
geometry would name from an anchor has no cell here and the door is
refused. A plane shared by several native levels is refused too, because
reviewed boundary walls enter level by level.

An accepted door becomes an ordinary connected door: the exported door
record, its portal (marked reviewed, edge evidence "reviewed-native-door",
accessibility unknown) and an info issue with the sides, cells and gaps.
An `observe` list evaluates the same predicate without changing anything.

nativeCirculationGeometryKey is not changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
